1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,585
The flag on the Puri temple flies against the wind,

2
00:00:03,585 --> 00:00:06,453
or so people say. The wind comes in from the sea,

3
00:00:06,453 --> 00:00:09,321
yet the flag flutters toward the sea.

4
00:00:09,321 --> 00:00:12,548
For centuries, pilgrims have folded their hands at this sight.

5
00:00:12,548 --> 00:00:16,850
And today, even weather scientists watch this flag closely.

6
00:00:16,850 --> 00:00:18,637
This is not the only mystery.

7
00:00:18,637 --> 00:00:21,855
They say the temple's shadow is never seen on the ground.

8
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:25,430
The wheel on the top looks straight at you from every direction.

9
00:00:25,430 --> 00:00:28,647
In the kitchen, the topmost pot cooks first.

10
00:00:28,647 --> 00:00:32,580
The moment you cross the Singhadwara, the sound of the sea goes silent.

11
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:36,514
In this video, with every mystery, you will get both sides.

12
00:00:36,514 --> 00:00:40,448
On one side, the devotee's faith; on the other, the calculation of science.

13
00:00:40,448 --> 00:00:44,382
We will not call anyone wrong. We will only lay out the evidence,

14
00:00:44,382 --> 00:00:48,710
and the decision will be yours. Come, let's go to the Odisha seashore.

15
00:00:48,710 --> 00:00:51,534
First, let's see what the scriptures say.

16
00:00:51,534 --> 00:00:54,357
The Skanda Purana has a section called Utkala Khanda.

17
00:00:54,357 --> 00:00:55,769
Utkala means old Odisha.

18
00:00:55,769 --> 00:00:59,652
In this section, the glory of Puri is written in detail.

19
00:00:59,652 --> 00:01:02,122
And here there is one very special point,

20
00:01:02,122 --> 00:01:04,240
which is the foundation of the whole story.

21
00:01:04,240 --> 00:01:07,458
The Skanda Purana calls Puri Purushottama Kshetra.

22
00:01:07,458 --> 00:01:10,275
Kshetra means a holy land, a place of pilgrimage.

23
00:01:10,275 --> 00:01:13,091
According to the scripture, God is everywhere.

24
00:01:13,091 --> 00:01:15,907
Even so, this kshetra is the greatest of all.

25
00:01:15,907 --> 00:01:19,930
Because this place has itself become the body of the Supreme Lord.

26
00:01:19,930 --> 00:01:22,092
Just feel this for a moment.

27
00:01:22,092 --> 00:01:25,694
For the scripture, Puri is not just a city with a temple.

28
00:01:25,694 --> 00:01:27,856
The sand here, the seashore,

29
00:01:27,856 --> 00:01:30,377
all of it is part of that divine form.

30
00:01:30,377 --> 00:01:34,340
That is why pilgrims here touch the ground and press it to their foreheads.

31
00:01:34,340 --> 00:01:37,323
Now a popular story, the kind grandmothers tell.

32
00:01:37,323 --> 00:01:40,680
A king saw the Lord in a dream.

33
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:43,663
A divine log came floating in the sea.

34
00:01:43,663 --> 00:01:45,901
The idols were made from that very log.

35
00:01:45,901 --> 00:01:49,630
This story has been passed down by word of mouth, generation after generation.

36
00:01:49,630 --> 00:01:51,135
This is why the idols of Jagannath,

37
00:01:51,135 --> 00:01:54,145
Balabhadra and Subhadra are made of wood.

38
00:01:54,145 --> 00:01:57,155
Not of stone or metal. Devotees say,

39
00:01:57,155 --> 00:01:59,789
this temple runs by its own rules.

40
00:01:59,789 --> 00:02:02,799
And it is from here that those mysteries begin,

41
00:02:02,799 --> 00:02:04,680
the ones we will walk behind today.

42
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:08,879
Now let's leave the scriptures and move into the world of measuring and testing.

43
00:02:08,879 --> 00:02:10,817
The Archaeological Survey of India, that is, ASI,

44
00:02:10,817 --> 00:02:13,402
looks after the country's old buildings.

45
00:02:13,402 --> 00:02:16,632
When did ASI take this temple into its hands?

46
00:02:16,632 --> 00:02:18,570
The answer is hidden in one year.

47
00:02:18,570 --> 00:02:19,741
The year was 1975.

48
00:02:19,741 --> 00:02:23,643
ASI took the Jagannath temple under national protection.

49
00:02:23,643 --> 00:02:27,546
Conservation means saving a building from falling apart and repairing it.

50
00:02:27,546 --> 00:02:30,668
This decision was made through a government notification.

51
00:02:30,668 --> 00:02:34,180
Since then, its walls have been looked after regularly.

52
00:02:34,180 --> 00:02:37,471
ASI's records consider it a temple many centuries old.

53
00:02:37,471 --> 00:02:39,665
Its structure is in the Kalinga style.

54
00:02:39,665 --> 00:02:42,956
Kalinga style means the special architecture of ancient Odisha.

55
00:02:42,956 --> 00:02:45,882
In it, the tower becomes thinner as it goes up,

56
00:02:45,882 --> 00:02:47,710
like the peak of a mountain.

57
00:02:47,710 --> 00:02:51,830
This kind of tall tower is called a Rekha Deula.

58
00:02:51,830 --> 00:02:55,949
Deula means the temple's sanctum and its tower. It is called Rekha because

59
00:02:55,949 --> 00:03:00,069
its walls rise upward in a curving line.

60
00:03:00,069 --> 00:03:04,600
This very curve will come in handy later in the mystery of the shadow.

61
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:08,317
And sitting at the very top of this tower is the Neela Chakra.

62
00:03:08,317 --> 00:03:12,405
It is considered a symbol of Lord Vishnu's Sudarshan chakra.

63
00:03:12,405 --> 00:03:16,122
According to ASI's records, it is made of ashtadhatu.

64
00:03:16,122 --> 00:03:20,210
Ashtadhatu means an alloy made by mixing several metals.

65
00:03:20,210 --> 00:03:22,875
And its size? Around 3.5 metres.

66
00:03:22,875 --> 00:03:26,428
That is, much bigger than even a tall man.

67
00:03:26,428 --> 00:03:30,870
Such a heavy metal wheel, on such a high tower. Just think,

68
00:03:30,870 --> 00:03:35,755
how it must have been lifted up there without today's machines.

69
00:03:35,755 --> 00:03:38,420
We will raise this same question again later.

70
00:03:38,420 --> 00:03:39,562
People say,

71
00:03:39,562 --> 00:03:42,989
every day a priest-servant climbs this tower.

72
00:03:42,989 --> 00:03:47,178
He takes down the old flag near the chakra and ties a new one.

73
00:03:47,178 --> 00:03:49,462
Using only his hands and feet.

74
00:03:49,462 --> 00:03:53,270
Devotees standing below hold their breath and watch this sight.

75
00:03:53,270 --> 00:03:56,328
Now the first big question, which every pilgrim asks.

76
00:03:56,328 --> 00:03:58,706
Why does the flag fly against the wind?

77
00:03:58,706 --> 00:04:02,104
On this, devotees and scientists say different things.

78
00:04:02,104 --> 00:04:05,501
Listen to both carefully. First the side of faith,

79
00:04:05,501 --> 00:04:07,200
then the calculation of weather science.

80
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:10,841
For devotees, the answer is simple. This is the Lord's divine play.

81
00:04:10,841 --> 00:04:13,490
A flag that moves against the laws of nature

82
00:04:13,490 --> 00:04:16,138
is a divine sign. Many pilgrims say

83
00:04:16,138 --> 00:04:19,780
they have seen it with their own eyes. Standing on the sand,

84
00:04:19,780 --> 00:04:23,090
sea wind on their face, and the flag flying the opposite way.

85
00:04:23,090 --> 00:04:26,017
Now, about the India Meteorological Department, that is, IMD.

86
00:04:26,017 --> 00:04:28,577
IMD is the country's official weather department.

87
00:04:28,577 --> 00:04:34,064
It says small local swirls of wind form along the eastern coast.

88
00:04:34,064 --> 00:04:38,820
Along with the larger weather, the sea breeze and heat together create these swirls.

89
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:43,303
Sea breeze means the cool wind that blows from the sea toward the land during the day.

90
00:04:43,303 --> 00:04:45,544
In the evening it often reverses,

91
00:04:45,544 --> 00:04:47,145
blowing from the land toward the sea.

92
00:04:47,145 --> 00:04:50,027
So the wind direction at the coast keeps changing.

93
00:04:50,027 --> 00:04:52,269
The wind you feel down below

94
00:04:52,269 --> 00:04:54,190
can be different up above.

95
00:04:54,190 --> 00:04:56,177
There is one more reason, the thermal eddy.

96
00:04:56,177 --> 00:05:00,150
A thermal eddy is a whirl of air spinning near a hot surface.

97
00:05:00,150 --> 00:05:03,131
The temple's curved spire gets hot in the sun.

98
00:05:03,131 --> 00:05:05,780
The air around it bends and spins.

99
00:05:05,780 --> 00:05:08,760
Up top, the flag flutters with this spinning air.

100
00:05:08,760 --> 00:05:10,005
So scientists say,

101
00:05:10,005 --> 00:05:13,738
the flag is actually flying with the wind up above.

102
00:05:13,738 --> 00:05:16,538
It's just that this wind is opposite to the wind on the ground.

103
00:05:16,538 --> 00:05:19,961
Devotees say even this explanation is part of the same divine play.

104
00:05:19,961 --> 00:05:22,450
Both views still go side by side today.

105
00:05:22,450 --> 00:05:24,905
The next mystery, the shadow. People say,

106
00:05:24,905 --> 00:05:29,112
at no time of day is the temple's shadow seen on the ground.

107
00:05:29,112 --> 00:05:32,970
Whether noon or evening, the spire's shadow doesn't fall on the sand.

108
00:05:32,970 --> 00:05:36,476
This is on the lips of every guide in Puri.

109
00:05:36,476 --> 00:05:38,580
But is it really so?

110
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:42,072
Analysts who work on Kalinga architecture say,

111
00:05:42,072 --> 00:05:43,623
the temple does cast a shadow.

112
00:05:43,623 --> 00:05:47,503
It's just that the shadow doesn't fall where we look for it.

113
00:05:47,503 --> 00:05:51,382
The spire of the Rekha Deula gets thinner as it goes up.

114
00:05:51,382 --> 00:05:53,710
Its walls are not straight, they are curved.

115
00:05:53,710 --> 00:05:56,620
The temple stands on a wide, high base.

116
00:05:56,620 --> 00:06:00,620
This is called a podium, that is, the raised platform under a building.

117
00:06:00,620 --> 00:06:04,257
The spire's shadow first falls on its own tiers.

118
00:06:04,257 --> 00:06:06,803
Tiers means layers like steps on the wall.

119
00:06:06,803 --> 00:06:10,440
Then on the walls of the platform and the roofs nearby.

120
00:06:10,440 --> 00:06:13,502
The temple is built in line with each main direction.

121
00:06:13,502 --> 00:06:17,925
That is why, at the steep angles of the sun, the shadow shrinks inward.

122
00:06:17,925 --> 00:06:20,647
In the open ground outside, no long shadow spreads.

123
00:06:20,647 --> 00:06:24,389
So to the eye, it looks like the shadow has disappeared. Analysts say,

124
00:06:24,389 --> 00:06:26,090
it is just hidden.

125
00:06:26,090 --> 00:06:28,739
Listen to the devotees' answer too. They say,

126
00:06:28,739 --> 00:06:31,719
such precise measurement centuries ago is itself a miracle.

127
00:06:31,719 --> 00:06:35,693
Someone planned the spire so carefully that even the shadow stays inside.

128
00:06:35,693 --> 00:06:40,660
Here, science and faith seem to be saying the same thing in different words.

129
00:06:40,660 --> 00:06:42,955
Now, the mystery of the Neela Chakra. They say,

130
00:06:42,955 --> 00:06:44,922
from anywhere in Puri you look,

131
00:06:44,922 --> 00:06:48,201
the chakra appears to be facing you. From the east,

132
00:06:48,201 --> 00:06:50,168
from the west, from any lane.

133
00:06:50,168 --> 00:06:53,119
As if it is looking straight at every devotee.

134
00:06:53,119 --> 00:06:56,070
Children also go around and play this game.

135
00:06:56,070 --> 00:06:58,852
ASI records tell an interesting thing.

136
00:06:58,852 --> 00:07:02,678
The outer rim of the chakra is open toward every main direction.

137
00:07:02,678 --> 00:07:07,199
Its structure is such that it looks almost the same from every side.

138
00:07:07,199 --> 00:07:09,286
So geometry, the mathematics of shapes,

139
00:07:09,286 --> 00:07:11,720
plays a big role in this feeling.

140
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:15,023
Still, for the devotee, this is not just a metal wheel.

141
00:07:15,023 --> 00:07:16,824
A flag is tied on the Neela Chakra,

142
00:07:16,824 --> 00:07:19,226
and people bow from far away.

143
00:07:19,226 --> 00:07:21,627
Many pilgrims are not able to go inside the temple.

144
00:07:21,627 --> 00:07:24,930
For them, seeing the chakra is considered the complete darshan.

145
00:07:24,930 --> 00:07:28,825
Now let's go to the temple kitchen, where the Mahaprasad is made.

146
00:07:28,825 --> 00:07:31,941
Mahaprasad means the sacred food offered to God.

147
00:07:31,941 --> 00:07:36,226
Here, clay pots are stacked one on top of another and cooked

148
00:07:36,226 --> 00:07:38,563
over a wood fire.

149
00:07:38,563 --> 00:07:40,900
And here is one more mystery.

150
00:07:40,900 --> 00:07:42,774
The kitchen workers say,

151
00:07:42,774 --> 00:07:45,772
the topmost pot cooks first.

152
00:07:45,772 --> 00:07:49,145
While the fire is at the very bottom. Seems backwards, doesn't it?

153
00:07:49,145 --> 00:07:53,642
The Centre for Culinary Heritage Documentation has recorded a discussion on this.

154
00:07:53,642 --> 00:07:57,390
On one side the cook's experience, on the other side questions of physics.

155
00:07:57,390 --> 00:08:00,105
Physicists say, this is the play of convection.

156
00:08:00,105 --> 00:08:04,178
Convection means hot steam rising up and carrying heat along with it.

157
00:08:04,178 --> 00:08:06,214
Clay pots are porous,

158
00:08:06,214 --> 00:08:08,250
meaning they have tiny holes in them.

159
00:08:08,250 --> 00:08:10,626
The steam rises up through these holes,

160
00:08:10,626 --> 00:08:13,680
and the whole stack becomes like a furnace.

161
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:16,930
How does the heat reach this furnace, and in what order?

162
00:08:16,930 --> 00:08:19,096
There is still debate about that.

163
00:08:19,096 --> 00:08:22,346
The cooks stand by what they say. Scientists say,

164
00:08:22,346 --> 00:08:24,873
without measurements, it's hard to say for sure.

165
00:08:24,873 --> 00:08:28,123
And the sound of the sea going silent at the Singhadwara?

166
00:08:28,123 --> 00:08:30,650
We have no measurement of that yet.

167
00:08:30,650 --> 00:08:34,319
Now, the things nobody knows even today.

168
00:08:34,319 --> 00:08:38,396
How was such a heavy wheel lifted onto such a high peak?

169
00:08:38,396 --> 00:08:42,880
There is no complete record of that medieval engineering method.

170
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:46,142
No plan, no written calculation.

171
00:08:46,142 --> 00:08:48,180
This question is still open.

172
00:08:48,180 --> 00:08:51,379
And one more open question: the air above the peak.

173
00:08:51,379 --> 00:08:53,157
How the air moves up there,

174
00:08:53,157 --> 00:08:56,000
a full scientific model of that has not been built yet.

175
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:59,200
A model means calculating the movement of air on a computer.

176
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:03,110
Until that is built, the story of the flag is incomplete.

177
00:09:03,110 --> 00:09:06,326
If you go to Puri today, what can you see?

178
00:09:06,326 --> 00:09:09,542
Stand on the seashore and watch the direction of the flag.

179
00:09:09,542 --> 00:09:11,686
Then feel the wind on your face.

180
00:09:11,686 --> 00:09:13,830
At noon, look for the shadow of the temple.

181
00:09:13,830 --> 00:09:17,760
And look at the Neela Chakra from different lanes, judge for yourself.

182
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:21,496
The temple's strong stone walls still stand today.

183
00:09:21,496 --> 00:09:24,484
The ASI has been maintaining them since 1975.

184
00:09:24,484 --> 00:09:27,846
As you walk toward the Singhadwara, listen to the sound of the sea.

185
00:09:27,846 --> 00:09:31,209
Decide for yourself what you feel.

186
00:09:31,209 --> 00:09:33,450
The evidence will be in front of you, the decision is yours.

187
00:09:33,450 --> 00:09:37,012
So which mystery attracts you the most? The reversed flag,

188
00:09:37,012 --> 00:09:39,505
the hidden shadow, or the wheel that watches from every side?

189
00:09:39,505 --> 00:09:41,642
Write just one word in the comments.

190
00:09:41,642 --> 00:09:43,778
And if you have been to Puri,

191
00:09:43,778 --> 00:09:47,340
do tell us what you saw with your own eyes.

192
00:09:47,340 --> 00:09:51,131
Next time we go to the seashore of Gujarat, Dwarka.

193
00:09:51,131 --> 00:09:55,765
They say a whole city sank into the water there. The gotakhor,

194
00:09:55,765 --> 00:09:58,714
that is, the divers, what did they find there?

195
00:09:58,714 --> 00:10:02,927
And what do scientists say about it? With evidence,

196
00:10:02,927 --> 00:10:05,033
we'll meet in the next story.
